== 5. robust feed simulation: a second connection B with independent drops
  observed outages (last frame -> next ack, s): [1.62, 1.19, 1.89, 31.72, 1.32]
  B with recorded reconnect: of the 22 season-225 losses, still lost (both down) mean 0.234, P(none lost) 0.9374, p99 9, max 21
  B with fast-retry reconnect: of the 22 season-225 losses, still lost (both down) mean 0.155, P(none lost) 0.9589, p99 5, max 20
  per season, recorded: P(lose >= 1 official advisory or damage report) 1 conn 0.250, 2 conns 0.0020; 1 conn mean lost official advisories 0.235, damage reports 0.0553
  per season (866 msgs), recorded: 1 conn loses mean 8.4 (P>0 0.79); 2 conns mean 0.088 (P>0 0.028)
  per season, fast-retry: P(lose >= 1 official advisory or damage report) 1 conn 0.190, 2 conns 0.0008; 1 conn mean lost official advisories 0.168, damage reports 0.0450
  per season (866 msgs), fast-retry: 1 conn loses mean 6.0 (P>0 0.64); 2 conns mean 0.052 (P>0 0.014)
  fast retry alone, conn 3: reconnect by s=481.33; saves 1 of 1
  fast retry alone, conn 4: reconnect between s=236.32 and 252.79; saves 0-11 of 20
  fast retry alone, conn 5: reconnect by s=451.31; saves 1 of 1
  => fast retry on one connection saves 2-13 of the 22 season-225 losses
  if the long outage was server-side (common to both connections), B saves only the 2 short-drop losses; a fast-retry policy would then still lose the messages published while the endpoint was unreachable (>= 15 s)

